<section class="workshop-hero">
  <div class="workshop-container">
    <a href="/labs" class="workshop-back">&larr; All engineering labs</a>
    <p class="workshop-eyebrow">Inference Collective / Workshop tracks</p>
    <h1>Learn by building.<br /><span>Keep what you create.</span></h1>
    <p class="workshop-lede">
      A clear path from your first command to a working result. Choose a track, run the code, inspect the output, and make it your own.
    </p>
    <div class="workshop-facts">
      <span>CPU &amp; Apple silicon tracks</span><span>Included datasets</span><span>No API keys</span><span>Self paced or instructor led</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="workshop-container workshop-section" aria-labelledby="tracks-title">
  <div class="workshop-section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="workshop-eyebrow">01 / Choose your outcome</p><h2 id="tracks-title">
        Your next working project
      </h2>
    </div><p>Times include setup and practice. Take the time you need.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="workshop-grid">
    <article
      :for={{track, index} <- Enum.with_index(@tracks, 1)}
      class="workshop-card"
      id={"track-#{track["id"]}"}
    >
      <div class="workshop-card-top">
        <span class="workshop-number">0{index}</span><span class="workshop-badge">{track["level"]}</span>
      </div>
      <h3><a href={~p"/workshops/#{track["id"]}"}>{track["title"]}</a></h3>
      <p>{track["description"]}</p>
      <div class="workshop-meta">
        ~{track["minutes"]} min · {length(track["steps"])} guided labs · {track["hardware"] ||
          "CPU"}
      </div>
      <ol class="workshop-preview">
        <li :for={step <- track["steps"]}>{step["title"]}</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="kube-button" href={~p"/workshops/#{track["id"]}"}>Start this track &rarr;</a>
      <small>Prerequisites: {track["prerequisites"]}</small>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="workshop-container workshop-section workshop-how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div>
    <p class="workshop-eyebrow">02 / A repeatable way to learn</p><h2 id="how-title">
      Run. Inspect. Change. Explain.
    </h2><p>
      Every track pairs existing source code with a concrete output and an extension exercise. Use the full guides whenever you need more background.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Set up once</strong><span>Choose macOS/Linux or Windows commands. Install only the packages your track needs.</span>
    </li><li>
      <strong>Build something observable</strong><span>Run one lab at a time. Compare the report or image with the expected outcome.</span>
    </li><li>
      <strong>Make it your own</strong><span>Change a parameter, rerun, and explain what changed before moving on.</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
<section class="workshop-container workshop-section workshop-callout">
  <div>
    <p class="workshop-eyebrow">Bring your team</p><h2>Run this as a workshop.</h2><p>
      Allow 10 minutes for setup, pair up for the labs, and close with a short demo. Progress stays in each participant’s browser when storage is available.
    </p>
  </div><a
    class="kube-button kube-button-outline"
    href="https://github.com/inferencecollective/inferencecollective.github.io/tree/main/labs"
  >Explore the source &nearr;</a>
</section>
